n: 4.3
name: knowledge-representation
kind: hub
is: A survey of knowledge representations against six requirements finds no prior system that meets all six and proposes immutable 'key: value' text blocks with ids computed from content, change by superseding nodes, derived views and hubs as bounded summaries. Published measurements: an edge list costs 2,645 tokens against 8,171 for Turtle and 13,503 for JSON-LD, at a higher score; key-value records scored 60.7% against JSON 52.3%. One claim is 333 bytes against 365 as compact JSON. Tokens, a local model's writing and merging were not tested.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 4.3.3
name: proposed-format
kind: hub
is: The reading's proposal and what was run for it: seven sentences that define a graph of immutable nodes, a block format of raw key-value lines with fourteen machine checks, three example ids recomputed as SHA-256 prefixes, one claim measured at 333 bytes against 365 as compact JSON, and git's union merge driver proposed for concurrent additions. No prior system met all six requirements. Token counts, a local model's writing and the merge were not tested.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 4.3.3.3
name: byte-and-hash-probe
kind: finding
is: The reading computed three example ids (c808c09b, 25d9086d, 7200e47a) as the first 8 hex digits of SHA-256 over each block's lines after the id line. One claim block measured 333 bytes as key-value lines, 365 as compact JSON, 407 as pretty JSON, and 465 or 601 as Turtle without or with its prefix lines; the statement sentence alone is 135 bytes.
status: assumed
limit: Bytes, not tokens, and one block.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 4.3.3.4
name: git-union-driver
kind: observation
is: Git's built-in union merge driver takes lines from both versions of a text file and leaves no conflict markers. Its manual says the added lines tend to end up in random order and that the user should verify the result.
status: observed
src: 2.13.39
at: 2026-11-24

n: 4.3.3.6
name: format-not-exercised
kind: finding
is: The proposed format was designed and not exercised: no tokenizer was run, no local model wrote or read the blocks, and 'merge=union' over files of immutable blocks was argued from git's manual and never tried.
status: inferred
conf: high
from: 4.3.3.3 4.3.3.4
at: 2026-11-24

